data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Validated recipe — uniswap-v4@4.0.0\n\n⚠ Version disagreement: this recipe was validated against `uniswap-v4@4.0.0`, while the units below are labelled `uniswap-v4@1.0.2`. Both are stated rather than reconciled — a recipe's stamp records what was actually run, and a unit's label records what the corpus holds. Differences inside one major are not always cosmetic: check the recipe's own pins before copying it against these units.\n_human-validated 2026-08-14 by farseen (github: FarseenSh)_\n_source: recipes/uniswap-v4/hook-swap.yaml_\n\n**Receipts** — what was actually run, on 2026-08-14, by farseen (github: FarseenSh)\n- checks: attest, test, fork\n- chains exercised: ethereum\n- on-chain:\n  - none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result.\n\n# Recipe: uniswap-v4 @4 :: hook-swap\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-14 by farseen (github: FarseenSh). 7 quotes · 9 structural · 6 fork assertions, all green. Stamped after the curator ran the check set on his own machine — see sources.json.\n# ⚠ SCOPE: THIS ROW BUILDS AND VERIFIES A HOOK — IT DOES NOT EXECUTE A SWAP. The type is\n#   `hook-swap` and the swap half is not authored; see scope_notes.not_covered.\n# ⚠ IN v4 A POOL HAS NO ADDRESS, AND THE HOOK IS PART OF THE POOL'S IDENTITY.\n#\n#   Every pool lives inside ONE singleton PoolManager and is named by a `PoolKey`\n#   {currency0, currency1, fee, tickSpacing, hooks}. The id is keccak256 over that whole\n#   struct — so the same pair, at the same fee, with a different hook, is A DIFFERENT POOL\n#   with different liquidity and a different price.\n#\n#     \"the USDC/ETH 0.05% pool\" DOES NOT IDENTIFY A v4 POOL.\n#\n# ⚠ THIS ROW MEASURES POOL IDENTITY AND THE LOCK DISCIPLINE. IT DOES NOT EXECUTE A SWAP —\n#   that needs a hook mined to an address whose low bits match its declared permissions, plus\n#   settle/take accounting. Stated here and in scope_notes rather than implied. See V-REJ2.\n#\n# Sources pinned 2026-08-15:\n#   Uniswap/v4-core @ e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba (tag v4.0.0)\n#   Uniswap/universal-router @ fb25ff09c71dcfc13665e6c65788db737f29e0d4 (the address, as a\n#     deploy PARAMETER — not a registry; see V-REJ3)\nproject_id: \"uniswap-v4\"    # ⚠ A SEPARATE project_id from `uniswap-v3`, per the locked worklist\n                            #   and the never-merge rule. Both are live; see V-REJ4.\nversion_major: 4\nversion: \"4.0.0\"            # the v4-core tag this recipe read. ⚠ The repo publishes exactly one\n                            #   version tag, `v4.0.0`, and that is what is pinned — a real\n                            #   released version of the thing that was read, not a generation.\ntype: \"hook-swap\"\n\n# ⚠ ETHEREUM ONLY. Everything was read on one mainnet fork; v4 is deployed more widely and this\n# recipe does not claim a chain it did not read.\nchains: [ethereum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ THE v3 FACTORY IS LISTED ON PURPOSE. It is live, it still answers `getPool`, and the whole\n# finding is that the two architectures coexist under one product name.#\n# ⚠ RE-KEYED BY CHAIN 2026-08-15 (F-4), labels preserved as the inner keys. No address value\n#   changed — verified by comparing the address multiset before and after. Placement is MEASURED:\n#   eth_getCode returned non-empty at each address on each chain listed here.\n# 🔴 THIS EDIT POSTDATES THE STAMP ABOVE. The stamp was not touched and this row needs a fresh\n#   curator run before launch; it is listed in the F-4 report for exactly that reason.\ndeployments:\n  ethereum:\n    v4_pool_manager: \"0x000000000004444c5dc75cB358380D2e3dE08A90\"\n    v3_factory_still_live: \"0x1F98431c8aD98523631AE4a59f267346ea31F984\"\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"uniswap-v4\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba/src/types/PoolKey.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── V4PoolIdentity.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    /// v4's pool key. Declared locally so the recipe pins the shape it was written against.\n    struct PoolKey {\n        address currency0;\n        address currency1;\n        uint24 fee;\n        int24 tickSpacing;\n        address hooks;\n    }\n\n    interface IPoolManagerMin {\n        function unlock(bytes calldata data) external returns (bytes memory);\n        function extsload(bytes32 slot) external view returns (bytes32);\n    }\n\n    interface IUnlockCallback {\n        function unlockCallback(bytes calldata data) external returns (bytes memory);\n    }\n\n    /// Everything a v4 integration has to get right BEFORE it swaps: which pool it means, and\n    /// how to be allowed to touch the manager at all.\n    ///\n    /// ⚠ This contract does not swap. It establishes identity and demonstrates the lock\n    ///   discipline — the two places a v3 habit produces a confident wrong answer.\n    contract V4PoolIdentity is IUnlockCallback {\n        /// ⚠ NAMED, not defaulted. v4 has one manager per chain and v3 has a factory; passing\n        ///   the wrong one is the failure this recipe is about, so it is never implicit.\n        address public immutable poolManager;\n\n        bool public lastUnlockRan;\n\n        error CurrenciesNotSorted(address currency0, address currency1);\n        error NotThePoolManager(address caller);\n\n        constructor(address poolManager_) {\n            poolManager = poolManager_;\n        }\n\n        /// The pool id — keccak256 over the WHOLE key, hook included.\n        ///\n        /// ⚠ There is no factory lookup and no pool address. Two keys that differ only in\n        ///   `hooks` are different pools, with different liquidity and different prices.\n        function idFor(PoolKey memory key) public pure returns (bytes32) {\n            if (uint160(key.currency0) >= uint160(key.currency1)) {\n                revert CurrenciesNotSorted(key.currency0, key.currency1);\n            }\n            return keccak256(abi.encode(key));\n        }\n\n        /// The same pair and fee, with and without a hook, are two pools. Returned together so\n        /// a caller can see it rather than be told it.\n        function idsWithAndWithoutHook(PoolKey memory key, address hook)\n            public\n            pure\n            returns (bytes32 withoutHook, bytes32 withHook)\n        {\n            PoolKey memory bare = key;\n            bare.hooks = address(0);\n            withoutHook = idFor(bare);\n\n            PoolKey memory hooked = key;\n            hooked.hooks = hook;\n            withHook = idFor(hooked);\n        }\n\n        /// ⚠ THE FEE FIELD IS NOT ALWAYS A FEE. The top bit set — exactly 0x800000 — declares a\n        ///   DYNAMIC fee pool. Reading that value as 8,388,608 pips is a 838% fee that does not\n        ///   exist.\n        function isDynamicFee(uint24 fee) public pure returns (bool) {\n            return fee == 0x800000;\n        }\n\n        /// Do something with the manager, correctly: unlock, and act inside the callback.\n        ///\n\n_… recipe truncated for budget — 30264 bytes total, full text at the source path above._\n_Continue it: `web3_fetch` with `cursor: \"recipe:uniswap-v4@4.0.0::hook-swap::body@6287\"` — each call returns the next slice and the next cursor until there is none._\n\n**Citations** (preserved through truncation — degrade bodies, never citations):\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba/src/types/PoolKey.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba/src/interfaces/IPoolManager.sol\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/tree/e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba\n- https://github.com/Uniswap/universal-router/tree/fb25ff09c71dcfc13665e6c65788db737f29e0d4\n\n---\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::V3Fuzzer::addLiquidity\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/PoolManager.swap.t.sol#L48-L93\n\n```\nfunction addLiquidity(\n        IUniswapV3Pool v3Pool,\n        PoolKey memory key_,\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~27\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L847-L877\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~3\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L234-L263\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~6\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L311-L340\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~9\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L387-L416\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~12\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L464-L493\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~15\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L541-L570\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~18\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L618-L647\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~21\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L694-L723\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```\n\n### uniswap-v4@1.0.2::HooksTest::__contract__~24\n`uniswap-v4@1.0.2` · ⚠ version_defaulted · repo:46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75 · as_of 2026-04-02T19:42:06Z\nhttps://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/46c6834698c48bc4a463a86d8420f4eb1d7f3b75/test/libraries/Hooks.t.sol#L770-L799\n\n```\nHooks.validateHookPermissions(\n            hookAddr,\n            Hooks.Permissions({\n```"}],"structuredContent":{"intent":"integrate","recipe":{"project_id":"uniswap-v4","version":"4.0.0","recipe_type":"hook-swap","last_validated":"2026-08-14","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","receipts":{"validated_on":"2026-08-14","validated_by":"farseen (github: FarseenSh)","checks":["attest","test","fork"],"chains_exercised":["ethereum"],"on_chain":"none recorded — this row exercises no chain, or its run broadcast nothing. A stated absence, never a gap: the receipt for such a row IS the suite result."},"body":"# Recipe: uniswap-v4 @4 :: hook-swap\n# STATUS: ✅ VALIDATED 2026-08-14 by farseen (github: FarseenSh). 7 quotes · 9 structural · 6 fork assertions, all green. Stamped after the curator ran the check set on his own machine — see sources.json.\n# ⚠ SCOPE: THIS ROW BUILDS AND VERIFIES A HOOK — IT DOES NOT EXECUTE A SWAP. The type is\n#   `hook-swap` and the swap half is not authored; see scope_notes.not_covered.\n# ⚠ IN v4 A POOL HAS NO ADDRESS, AND THE HOOK IS PART OF THE POOL'S IDENTITY.\n#\n#   Every pool lives inside ONE singleton PoolManager and is named by a `PoolKey`\n#   {currency0, currency1, fee, tickSpacing, hooks}. The id is keccak256 over that whole\n#   struct — so the same pair, at the same fee, with a different hook, is A DIFFERENT POOL\n#   with different liquidity and a different price.\n#\n#     \"the USDC/ETH 0.05% pool\" DOES NOT IDENTIFY A v4 POOL.\n#\n# ⚠ THIS ROW MEASURES POOL IDENTITY AND THE LOCK DISCIPLINE. IT DOES NOT EXECUTE A SWAP —\n#   that needs a hook mined to an address whose low bits match its declared permissions, plus\n#   settle/take accounting. Stated here and in scope_notes rather than implied. See V-REJ2.\n#\n# Sources pinned 2026-08-15:\n#   Uniswap/v4-core @ e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba (tag v4.0.0)\n#   Uniswap/universal-router @ fb25ff09c71dcfc13665e6c65788db737f29e0d4 (the address, as a\n#     deploy PARAMETER — not a registry; see V-REJ3)\nproject_id: \"uniswap-v4\"    # ⚠ A SEPARATE project_id from `uniswap-v3`, per the locked worklist\n                            #   and the never-merge rule. Both are live; see V-REJ4.\nversion_major: 4\nversion: \"4.0.0\"            # the v4-core tag this recipe read. ⚠ The repo publishes exactly one\n                            #   version tag, `v4.0.0`, and that is what is pinned — a real\n                            #   released version of the thing that was read, not a generation.\ntype: \"hook-swap\"\n\n# ⚠ ETHEREUM ONLY. Everything was read on one mainnet fork; v4 is deployed more widely and this\n# recipe does not claim a chain it did not read.\nchains: [ethereum]\n\n# ── THE DEPLOYMENTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ⚠ THE v3 FACTORY IS LISTED ON PURPOSE. It is live, it still answers `getPool`, and the whole\n# finding is that the two architectures coexist under one product name.#\n# ⚠ RE-KEYED BY CHAIN 2026-08-15 (F-4), labels preserved as the inner keys. No address value\n#   changed — verified by comparing the address multiset before and after. Placement is MEASURED:\n#   eth_getCode returned non-empty at each address on each chain listed here.\n# 🔴 THIS EDIT POSTDATES THE STAMP ABOVE. The stamp was not touched and this row needs a fresh\n#   curator run before launch; it is listed in the F-4 report for exactly that reason.\ndeployments:\n  ethereum:\n    v4_pool_manager: \"0x000000000004444c5dc75cB358380D2e3dE08A90\"\n    v3_factory_still_live: \"0x1F98431c8aD98523631AE4a59f267346ea31F984\"\n\n# ── WORKING EXAMPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworking_example:\n  source_protocol: \"uniswap-v4\"\n  source_url: \"https://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba/src/types/PoolKey.sol\"\n  code: |\n    // ── V4PoolIdentity.sol ──\n    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n    pragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\n    /// v4's pool key. Declared locally so the recipe pins the shape it was written against.\n    struct PoolKey {\n        address currency0;\n        address currency1;\n        uint24 fee;\n        int24 tickSpacing;\n        address hooks;\n    }\n\n    interface IPoolManagerMin {\n        function unlock(bytes calldata data) external returns (bytes memory);\n        function extsload(bytes32 slot) external view returns (bytes32);\n    }\n\n    interface IUnlockCallback {\n        function unlockCallback(bytes calldata data) external returns (bytes memory);\n    }\n\n    /// Everything a v4 integration has to get right BEFORE it swaps: which pool it means, and\n    /// how to be allowed to touch the manager at all.\n    ///\n    /// ⚠ This contract does not swap. It establishes identity and demonstrates the lock\n    ///   discipline — the two places a v3 habit produces a confident wrong answer.\n    contract V4PoolIdentity is IUnlockCallback {\n        /// ⚠ NAMED, not defaulted. v4 has one manager per chain and v3 has a factory; passing\n        ///   the wrong one is the failure this recipe is about, so it is never implicit.\n        address public immutable poolManager;\n\n        bool public lastUnlockRan;\n\n        error CurrenciesNotSorted(address currency0, address currency1);\n        error NotThePoolManager(address caller);\n\n        constructor(address poolManager_) {\n            poolManager = poolManager_;\n        }\n\n        /// The pool id — keccak256 over the WHOLE key, hook included.\n        ///\n        /// ⚠ There is no factory lookup and no pool address. Two keys that differ only in\n        ///   `hooks` are different pools, with different liquidity and different prices.\n        function idFor(PoolKey memory key) public pure returns (bytes32) {\n            if (uint160(key.currency0) >= uint160(key.currency1)) {\n                revert CurrenciesNotSorted(key.currency0, key.currency1);\n            }\n            return keccak256(abi.encode(key));\n        }\n\n        /// The same pair and fee, with and without a hook, are two pools. Returned together so\n        /// a caller can see it rather than be told it.\n        function idsWithAndWithoutHook(PoolKey memory key, address hook)\n            public\n            pure\n            returns (bytes32 withoutHook, bytes32 withHook)\n        {\n            PoolKey memory bare = key;\n            bare.hooks = address(0);\n            withoutHook = idFor(bare);\n\n            PoolKey memory hooked = key;\n            hooked.hooks = hook;\n            withHook = idFor(hooked);\n        }\n\n        /// ⚠ THE FEE FIELD IS NOT ALWAYS A FEE. The top bit set — exactly 0x800000 — declares a\n        ///   DYNAMIC fee pool. Reading that value as 8,388,608 pips is a 838% fee that does not\n        ///   exist.\n        function isDynamicFee(uint24 fee) public pure returns (bool) {\n            return fee == 0x800000;\n        }\n\n        /// Do something with the manager, correctly: unlock, and act inside the callback.\n        ///","source_path":"recipes/uniswap-v4/hook-swap.yaml","requested_version":null,"exact_version_match":null,"body_truncated":true,"body_bytes":30264,"citations":["https://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba/src/types/PoolKey.sol","https://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/blob/e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba/src/interfaces/IPoolManager.sol","https://github.com/Uniswap/v4-core/tree/e50237c43811bd9b526eff40f26772152a42daba","https://github.com/Uniswap/universal-router/tree/fb25ff09c71dcfc13665e6c65788db737f29e0d4"],"citations_capped":false,"body_cursor":"recipe:uniswap-v4@4.0.0::hook-swap::body@6287","version_note":"⚠ Version disagreement: this recipe was validated against `uniswap-v4@4.0.0`, while the units below are labelled `uniswap-v4@1.0.2`. Both are stated rather than reconciled — a recipe's stamp records what was actually run, and a unit's label records what the corpus holds. Differences inside one major are not always cosmetic: check the recipe's own pins before copying it against these units."},"hits":